{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"883","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L. Berland.Taxi"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Berland.Taxi is a new taxi company with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" cars which started operating in the capital of Berland just recently. The capital has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" houses on a straight line numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" (leftmost) to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" (rightmost), and the distance between any two neighboring houses is the same."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to help the company schedule all the taxi rides which come throughout the day according to the following rules: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" All cars are available for picking up passengers. Initially the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th car is located next to the house with the number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xj"},{"kind":"text","text":" at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" All cars have the same speed. It takes exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" minute for any car to travel between neighboring houses "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th request for taxi ride comes at the time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":", asking for a passenger to be picked up at the house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and dropped off at the house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":". All requests for taxi rides are given in the increasing order of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":". All "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" are distinct. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When a request for taxi ride is received at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":", Berland.Taxi operator assigns a car to it as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Out of cars which are currently available, operator assigns the car which is the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"closest"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the pick up spot "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":". Needless to say, if a car is already on a ride with a passenger, it won't be available for any rides until that passenger is dropped off at the corresponding destination. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If there are several such cars, operator will pick one of them which "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"has been waiting the most"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" since it became available. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If there are several such cars, operator will pick one of them which "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"has the lowest number"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After a car gets assigned to the taxi ride request: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The driver immediately starts driving from current position to the house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Once the car reaches house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":", the passenger is immediately picked up and the driver starts driving to house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Once house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is reached, the passenger gets dropped off and the car becomes available for new rides staying next to the house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" It is allowed for multiple cars to be located next to the same house at the same point in time, while waiting for ride requests or just passing by. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are no available cars at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" when a request for taxi ride comes, then: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th passenger will have to wait for a car to become available. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" When a car becomes available, operator will immediately assign it to this taxi ride request. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If multiple cars become available at once while the passenger is waiting, operator will pick a car out of them according to the rules described above. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Operator processes taxi ride requests one by one. So if multiple passengers are waiting for the cars to become available, operator will not move on to processing the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i + 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th ride request until the car gets assigned to the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th ride request."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to write a program that will process the given list of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" taxi ride requests. For each request you have to find out which car will get assigned to it, and how long the passenger will have to wait for a car to arrive. Note, if there is already car located at the house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the corresponding wait time will be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 2·105"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ k, m ≤ 2·105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — number of houses, number of cars, and number of taxi ride requests. The second line contains integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1, x2, ..., xk"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ xi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — initial positions of cars. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a house number at which the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th car is located initially. It's allowed for more than one car to be located next to the same house."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain information about ride requests. Each ride request is represented by integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"tj"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aj"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bj"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ tj ≤ 1012"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ aj, bj ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aj ≠ bj"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"tj"},{"kind":"text","text":" is time in minutes when a request is made, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aj"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a house where passenger needs to be picked up, and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bj"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a house where passenger needs to be dropped off. All taxi ride requests are given in the increasing order of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"tj"},{"kind":"text","text":". All "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"tj"},{"kind":"text","text":" are distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines: the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line should contain two integer numbers, the answer for the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th ride request — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"car number"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" assigned by the operator and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"passenger wait time"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 1 2\n3\n5 2 8\n9 10 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1\n1 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 2 1\n1 5\n10 3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 2 2\n1 5\n10 3 5\n20 4 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2\n2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample test, a request comes in at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the car needs to get from house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" to house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" to pick up the passenger. Therefore wait time will be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the ride will be completed at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5 + 1 + 6 = 12"},{"kind":"text","text":". The second request comes in at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"9"},{"kind":"text","text":", so the passenger will have to wait for the car to become available at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"12"},{"kind":"text","text":", and then the car needs another "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes to get from house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"8"},{"kind":"text","text":" to house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":". So the total wait time is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 + 2 = 5"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample test, cars "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" are located at the same distance from the first passenger and have the same \"wait time since it became available\". Car "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" wins a tiebreaker according to the rules because it has the lowest number. It will come to house "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", so the wait time will be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"L","problemCode":"883L","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/883/problem/L"}